WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.770
GeaNaVid checks claims against
the official Swiss voting booklet.

2
00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:08.091
Swiss voters hear claims like this one:

3
00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:11.401
the population has grown
by half a million since 2002.

4
00:00:11.451 --> 00:00:14.270
Is that what the official
voting booklet says?

5
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.624
GeaNaVid checks it.

6
00:00:16.674 --> 00:00:21.057
The answer is Gea, Na or Vid –
Romansh for yes, no and blank:

7
00:00:21.107 --> 00:00:26.285
the booklet supports the claim,
contradicts it, or says nothing about it.

8
00:00:26.335 --> 00:00:30.387
Every Gea and Na comes
with the passage that decides it.

9
00:00:30.437 --> 00:00:32.372
It is not voting advice.

10
00:00:33.122 --> 00:00:36.438
A German claim against the German booklet.

11
00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:39.663
The booklet says 1.7 million, on page 4,

12
00:00:39.713 --> 00:00:43.169
so the expected answer is Na:
contradiction.

13
00:00:43.219 --> 00:00:47.095
Every answer also reports
its tokens and its time.

14
00:00:47.845 --> 00:00:52.696
Now a German claim against the French
edition, a real case from OST's benchmark.

15
00:00:52.746 --> 00:00:55.716
Apertus first translates
the claim into French,

16
00:00:55.766 --> 00:00:58.452
then GeaNaVid searches the French booklet.

17
00:00:58.502 --> 00:01:01.985
The evidence stays in French,
straight from the booklet.

18
00:01:02.735 --> 00:01:06.014
Most of the work is choosing what to read.

19
00:01:06.064 --> 00:01:10.106
GeaNaVid first finds
the proposal the claim is about,

20
00:01:10.156 --> 00:01:13.228
then reads only its five best passages:

21
00:01:13.278 --> 00:01:16.834
about 1,500 tokens
per claim with Apertus 70B,

22
00:01:16.884 --> 00:01:20.025
instead of 20,000 for the whole booklet.

23
00:01:20.775 --> 00:01:29.013
We confirmed it on 497 held-out claims
from 21 booklets, with OST's human labels.

24
00:01:29.063 --> 00:01:35.491
With the whole booklet,
Apertus 8B reaches a macro F1 of 0.72.

25
00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:37.491
GeaNaVid: 0.96.

26
00:01:37.541 --> 00:01:43.588
70B: 0.97, against 0.89, with about
a tenth of the tokens.

27
00:01:44.338 --> 00:01:46.382
GeaNaVid runs on Apertus.

28
00:01:46.432 --> 00:01:50.368
Gea, Na or Vid,
always with the line that decides it.
